WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.980
Episode 2

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.980
We Don't Know a Thing

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.120
Nice job, Hayashi-kun!

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:44.410
Amber Volt!

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:03.260
Guess it's no surprise no one from the 
guild's online in the middle of the day.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:05.580
They're all working adults, after all.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.840
Y-Yeah, that's true.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.270
Speaking of, Hayashi-kun...

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.150
<i>I know where this conversation's going.</i>

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.400
You're always online.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.500
Are you a NEET?

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:24.540
<i>I-I'm an elite who </i>chose<i> the 
NEET lifestyle for myself.</i>

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.910
<i>An elite NEET!</i>

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.200
Speaking of, Hayashi-kun...

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.940
You're always online.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:36.940
Are you a university student?

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:41.780
Our guild, @Home Party,

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:45.060
has quite a few members who 
log on in the evenings.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:48.270
But I guess you could say it gets
 a bit lonely the rest of the day.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:52.680
So maybe I'm just happy that you're 
<i>always</i> online from early in the day.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.040
And so...

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.920
If I had to guess how 
old you are in real life,

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.530
I'd say you're the same age as me, 21!

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:04.960
She's so young!

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:05.700
<b>The thirties!</b>

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.830
S-So you're 21 years old?

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.250
Yup! Gotta go job hunting this year.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:13.520
So? You?

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.640
I-I'm...

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.770
A-Actually...

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:19.520
Thi...

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:20.300
Thi?

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:22.590
Th-Th...

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:23.300
<b>The thirties!</b>

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:27.060
Th-Thinking job hunting is 
gonna be a lot of work!

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.080
I-I'm in the same boat. It's rough!

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:34.720
We really are the same age! I'm super happy!

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:36.320
Me too, me too.

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.080
<i>I'm sorry. I'm sorry.</i>

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.320
<b>The thirties!</b>

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.320
<b>And a woman!</b>

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.880
So you're a university student?

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.740
H-How do you know that?

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.090
Everyone was really excited.

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:06.600
Listen to this!

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:09.600
Hayashi-kun really is a university student!

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.350
What? That's strange.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.060
I thought he was pretty...

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.660
Wow, he sure is young!

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.610
I don't even remember what 
it's like to be that young.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.610
So I'm the one who wins the bet!

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:25.740
Damn. And I was so sure 
he was in his late twenties...

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.130
Here. A million gold.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.250
Nice doing business with you!

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:36.800
That's all.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:40.980
I never thought they were betting on me...

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.690
I have to admit I was surprised
 to find out you're so young.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.140
Y-Yeah, that's right.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:49.140
How old do I seem?

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:51.930
I have no real basis for saying this,

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:54.140
but I thought you were a bit older than me.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:55.730
Jeez!

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:58.920
But if you're a university student,

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:02.090
that means you've got a lot 
hard work to look forward to.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.340
You're just so young. That's great.

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:10.440
<i>There's no going back now.</i>

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:15.520
<i>But while I do feel guilty about 
this lie spreading to more people,</i>

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:19.870
<i>I'm glad I won't need to dodge 
questions about my age anymore.</i>

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.900
<i>I never planned to ask before, but now...</i>

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:26.290
I wonder how old you are, Lily-san.

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:32.430
Crap. I just typed out what I was thinking.

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:36.940
This is bad. The awkward silence...

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.500
I really stepped on a landmine here.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:43.030
So you're curious, too...

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:45.410
Um, well...

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.490
You want to know about 
the private life of someone

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:51.590
you don't even know outside of a video game?

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:56.460
Don't you think there are things 
you're better off not knowing?

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:01.580
It was just a joke! A joke!

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:04.430
Please stop spamming the cry emote!

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.300
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:10.470
Okay?

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:16.290
But you know what? I know that Li-chan 
asked lightheartedly enough,

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:18.850
but it's really bad manners to pry like that.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:22.410
And on top of that, 
betting on it is unacceptable,

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.500
no matter how nice you are about it!

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:25.890
They're heartless!

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:28.570
Right?

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:32.850
That being said, I have to admit
 that I was somewhat interested myself.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:34.980
I guess I can't judge.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.570
I'm sorry.

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:39.370
No! Don't apologize.

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.320
But...

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:48.080
I think it might be okay to tell you 
a bit about myself in secret.

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:52.390
Hayashi-san?

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.390
Hayashi-san? Hayashi-san?

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:57.890
Hayashi-san!

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:06.570
I-It's true that I do want

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:10.490
to know more about you.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:19.000
But there are lots of things I'm not 
comfortable talking about myself,

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:22.400
so one day once we're a little closer...

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:24.060
Um...

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:30.050
You're just the kind of 
person I thought you were.

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:32.270
Serious and kindhearted.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.930
<i>Now I've got this vague sense of guilt...</i>

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:37.040
All right then.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:40.310
We'll have this talk again when we're 
closer to each other. For sure.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:42.850
Right!

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:46.040
It's a promise.

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:58.290
Also, I hope you don't think 
poorly of Kanbe-san for this.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:03.880
Putting the bet aside, he's the kind of 
person who really holds his friends dear.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:09.640
A little while back, the 
guild nearly disbanded.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:12.220
It did?

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:14.610
Yes.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:20.430
The previous guildmaster got 
a new job assignment overseas.

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:23.840
I know everyone will be sad if I quit.

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:26.910
But even so,

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:29.820
we haven't recruited any new members these 
past few months under my leadership!

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:33.160
Now... Now there's no choice but to end it!

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.700
<b>Disband the guild?</b>

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.700
Yes

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.700
No

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:41.090
Everyone, I'm really sorry.

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.660
Wait, wait, wait!

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.830
Transfer your authority to me.

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:48.980
It's true that we don't have many 
people online for very long,

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:51.230
but there are still people here!

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:53.170
Kanbe-san...

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.550
And besides...

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:59.050
It's such a waste to throw 
out a max level guild!

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:00.510
Oh.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:01.840
So that's it.

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:06.310
And well, that's how it went.

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:09.920
Because Kanbe-san took over the 
guild, we're all still here.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.320
That really is just like him.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.630
Is this supposed to be a positive story?

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:18.160
Thinking back on it now,

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:20.200
I don't think he did it for the guild level.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:23.870
I think he did it for all our friends
 that can't log in all the time.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.610
<i>Ah, I get it now.</i>

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:31.220
<i>Now I see why Kanbe-san is so 
satisfied with his online life.</i>

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:37.680
What's this?!

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:41.890
It's already 5:00?!

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:49.770
Lily-san! Lily-san!

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:51.680
Don't you have work today?

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.490
Huh? It's already 5:00!

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:56.260
I have to be in at 9:00 today!

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:58.090
You can still get a bit of sleep!

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:01.150
I have absolutely zero confidence 
that I'll wake up on time.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:05.160
Now that it's this late, 
I'll have to just stay up all night.

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:08.600
I'll accompany you as long as I possibly can.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:16.830
It's cold.

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:24.110
I fell asleep in the middle 
of playing and caught a cold.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:28.300
I've gotta get to a pharmacy 
and buy some medicine.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:32.380
No, I'm really very sorry.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:33.270
I'm going as fast as I can!

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:38.780
Anyway, today I'll...

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:40.850
I'll work nonstop, no breaks!

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:52.710
M-Ma'am?!

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.660
You're first to arrive again today.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.570
And you even stayed overtime yesterday.

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:21.260
Are you okay?

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:28.670
Yup. I want to make sure I 
get everything done at work.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:37.480
What <i>is</i> that?

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:58.890
Where's everyone going?

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:31.960
<i>Where am I?</i>

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:35.430
<i>Who's he?!</i>

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.740
<i>He has such pretty blond hair.</i>

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:40.100
<i>And it looks natural.</i>

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:41.360
<i>Wait, that's not important!</i>

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:46.320
Hello.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.370
<i>What in the world is going on?!</i>

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:52.370
Be careful with your arm.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:53.370
Huh?

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:55.680
You have an IV drip attached.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:57.130
<i>Don't tell me I'm in a hospital!</i>

00:12:58.030 --> 00:13:02.740
Um, I know I must be causing 
you a lot of trouble,

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:03.840
but what's going on?

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:08.240
This morning, I ran into you 
while going around a corner

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:09.480
and elbowed you.

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:11.390
<i>How the heck did you elbow me?</i>

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:14.180
I'm terribly sorry.

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:17.900
I had them examine you to make
 sure there was no head trauma.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:19.810
They told me you were fine.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:21.900
But I'm sure it still hurts...

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.930
I'm so sorry! Are you okay?

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.410
No, no, I'm perfectly fine!

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:30.410
I'm pretty tough.

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:33.070
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:35.510
That being said, you have a cold, don't you?

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:39.040
You can get a prescription for that here.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:40.440
Right.

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:43.920
Oh, but I don't have my health 
insurance card with me at the moment.

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:47.020
Please allow me to cover for you today.

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:49.460
I haven't introduced myself yet, have I?

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:52.410
Where's my business card case?

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:55.290
J-Just a moment...

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:56.350
Huh?

00:13:57.650 --> 00:13:59.740
<i>He's really fun to watch for some reason.</i>

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:00.940
Please accept this for now.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:01.690
Sakurai Yuta

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:04.690
Allow me to introduce myself.
 I'm Sakurai Yuta.

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:08.460
Please feel free to contact me 
if you're ever feeling unwell.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:10.310
I'll answer anytime I'm not sleeping.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:14.700
Sakurai Yuta

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:14.180
<i>Surprisingly, he's got a solid Japanese name.</i>

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:16.980
<i>Sakurai Yuta.</i>

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:18.650
<i>What a cute name.</i>

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:21.840
You've done so much for me.
 Thank you very much.

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:26.590
If you don't mind, could 
you tell me your name?

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:31.090
<b>Morioka Moriko</b>

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:31.090
<i>In comparison, my name sounds like a joke.</i>

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:34.770
I'm Morioka Moriko.

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:38.800
Morioka Moriko-san?

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:49.110
Sakurai Yuta

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:00.130
What's the matter? Why so blue?

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:02.080
Himeralda-san.

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:04.380
You look a little down.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:05.580
Gonna jump in?

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:08.130
No way. I'm not jumping.

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:10.220
Why do you look disappointed?!

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:15.720
I've just got a cold and sort of 
got wrapped up thinking about things.

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:22.050
If you're up to talking 
about it, we're all ears.

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:24.730
We might not be of much help, though.

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:27.500
But maybe you should ask Lilac to leave.

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:28.650
She's pretty loose-lipped!

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:32.210
What? Come on, even I wouldn't go 
blabbing about someone's problems!

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:33.360
You sure?

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:35.250
Come on, you two.

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:37.300
You're putting Hayashi-kun in a bind.

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:39.940
In any event, all we can do is listen,

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:42.750
but aren't we all friends here?

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:48.250
Thank you very much! Thank you very much!

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:57.740
Gosh, all I'm hearing is a setup 
for a romance manga plot!

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:01.140
How can you say you just want 
to give an update and thank her?

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:02.950
Yeah...

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:06.030
<i>This is what I get for flipping the genders 
and just giving them the rundown.</i>

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:08.770
<i>They're treating it like a 
love story for some reason!</i>

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:13.610
If you're a man, you've got to be upfront 
and take her out to dinner as thanks!

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.300
And then if you get lucky... 
If you get lucky, Hayashi-kun...

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:17.910
<b>The Carnivore</b>

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:17.910
If I get lucky, then what?!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.430
That's not how it works, Hime-chan.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:22.310
Imagine a weak herbivore of a man with 
an career woman older than himself.

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:24.230
He's not good with words 
and doesn't say much,

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:27.810
but he unexpectedly lifts up her head
 and just stares into her eyes.

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:30.740
Then she'll ask, "What is it?"
 He'll slowly inch closer to her,

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:34.190
and it will feel like time's moving in slow 
motion. Then she'll see how manly he is!

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:35.240
And then...

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:39.690
<i>Jeez, I have no idea what you're 
even talking about anymore.</i>

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:40.350
No.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.920
Normally it's polite to just send an email

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:45.090
or give a call to say thanks
 and be done with it.

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:46.350
<i>The voice of reason!</i>

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:47.710
That's totally boring!

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:48.810
Just boring!

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:50.860
<i>You guys are just having fun
 with this, aren't you?</i>

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:54.730
I don't know why you're hesitating,

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:56.860
but it's not good to leave 
her worried about you.

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:59.450
Try standing in her shoes. Got it?

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.150
<i>H-He's absolutely right.</i>

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:03.070
Yeah.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:04.440
All right.

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:05.850
I'll go email her.

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:06.990
<b>Away From Keyboard</b>

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.370
<b>Away From Keyboard</b>

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:17.970
It's been a long time since 
I've sent anyone an email.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:19.890
I'm nervous.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:21.890
But...

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:23.120
All right!

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:31.270
Pardon me a moment.

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:35.900
What's with that grin?

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:37.910
This? Or maybe this?

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:40.150
Koiwai-san, that makes you 
sound like an old man.

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:43.200
You're so cold, Sakura-chan.

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:55.300
When I think about how hard 
Hayashi-kun's working on that email,

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:57.760
it kind of makes me feel at peace.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:02.350
I'm not sure how I feel about you 
turning this into a romance plot.

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:06.810
But if it ends up turning into one,
 don't you think that would be wonderful?

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:11.690
<b>Away From Keyboard</b>

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:08.580
This isn't a manga.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:14.400
Welcome back.

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:17.610
I have returned...

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.070
What happened?!

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:21.950
Did something bad happen?!

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:25.700
Well, she replied right away.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:30.280
She said she wanted to apologize, 
so we should go out to eat sometime.

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:33.470
You might get lucky!
You just might get lucky, Hayashi-kun!

00:18:34.740 --> 00:18:36.590
Cut it out!

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:40.480
I don't want to!

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:43.090
Even going to the convenience
 store is a pain.

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:46.350
And he was so cool...

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:49.490
Blinding!

00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:59.520
<i>Unstyled hair, no makeup, unkempt eyebrows.</i>

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:02.280
<i>This is terrible!</i>

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:05.360
<i>C-Could this get any worse?</i>

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:11.290
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:16.170
No, I just got here.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:23.630
<i>Someone put a mosaic blur or a 
correction filter in front of his eyes!</i>

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:30.120
All right, it's MMO time.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:30.810
<b>And Moriko stopped thinking</b>

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:38.490
It looks like something's got you down.

00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:45.850
Lily-san!

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:55.270
Last year, I was the one sitting 
here feeling all down, wasn't I?

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:56.810
I guess that's true.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:03.550
When I'm feeling tired from work 
or when I have a bit of a bad day,

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:05.430
I often come here.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:09.770
I don't really have anyone 
to complain to in real life,

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:14.730
and I hate ruining the mood when
 everyone logs in to have a good time.

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:16.840
So usually,

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:19.090
I end up coming here to brood on my own.

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:20.930
But...

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:28.160
It looks like we're in the 
same boat as of today.

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:34.150
Let's keep it our little secret.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:43.010
<i>For some reason, I feel really 
warm right around here.</i>

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:47.640
Would you mind if I vented 
to you every so often?

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:51.100
Feel free! I'll keep it secret for sure!

00:20:51.340 --> 00:20:56.070
In return, I want you to rely on me more.

00:20:56.530 --> 00:20:57.770
It's a promise.

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:11.150
I better send a reply.

00:21:12.190 --> 00:21:16.930
<i>Lily is always so bright and cheerful, 
but even she has her own worries.</i>

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:20.840
<i>And yet she still goes out of 
her way for someone like me.</i>

00:21:21.430 --> 00:21:22.960
<i>Same with everyone else in our guild.</i>

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:27.180
<i>And even that man I met.</i>

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:31.180
Sakurai Yuta

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:30.820
<i>I have to give him a proper reply.</i>

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:34.680
Whatever happens... happens!

00:21:40.550 --> 00:21:42.430
It's 2:00 in the middle of the night!

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:44.430
I'm being a huge pain!

00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:47.340
Now I've done it!

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:40.230
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:27.100
I don't want to cause you any more trouble...

00:23:27.100 --> 00:23:29.590
I can see why that'd make you hesitate!

00:23:29.590 --> 00:23:32.210
Don't get any closer to him.

00:23:32.210 --> 00:23:33.590
I'm sorry.

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:39.430
Episode 3, "You and I, the Cowards."

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:40.230
<b>Episode 3 
You and I, the Cowards</b>
